--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Secret Service
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The protocol these bindings speak is the freedesktop Secret Service
specification. It is a specification rather than code, and nothing of it is
included here.

  https://specifications.freedesktop.org/secret-service-spec/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
On Fractal
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fractal is a GTK Matrix client, and the reason this binding exists: it drives
oo7 rather than libsecret, and reading it shows which operations a session
store needs -- unlock the collection, search by attribute, unlock each item.

It appears in no part of this product. It is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later, which
is incompatible with the Apache License this work is distributed under, so no
code or comment may be copied from it. Reading it to learn which operations a
flow needs is fine; carrying its expression across is not.

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/World/fractal
